              "directive": "When the judge has convicted a delivered result, locate the responsible step at the event that first introduced the contradicted delivered value into the trajectory — normally the final answer or final synthesis step — whenever that delivered value contradicts the trajectory's own tool observations, search results, or earlier prose; name that delivery event explicitly and cite the observation it contradicts.",
              "not_when": "Do not relocate responsibility to an upstream search or tool step whose observation already contains the correct value that the delivered answer contradicts, and do not name the delivery step when the wrong value already appears in an earlier tool observation or prose event; in that case keep the earliest event carrying the wrong value as the responsible step."
            },
            "claim": {
              "expected_behavior": "On judge-convicted cases whose delivered result contradicts the trajectory's own observations, the tracer names the final delivery/synthesis step that introduced the contradicted value as the responsible step instead of an upstream search or tool step whose evidence was correct.",
              "target_polarity": "boundary",
              "target_kind": "localization"
            },
