            "body": {
              "directive": "When the judge has flagged the delivered result as hallucinated, set responsibility by comparing the flagged claim against the trajectory's recorded tool observations. If the flagged claim contradicts an observation, or asserts a value that no observation supports, the responsible step is the assistant delivery step that first states the flagged claim: the final answer tool call whose arguments contain the delivered claim, or, when no answer tool call exists, the last prose event stating the delivered result. Name that step by its event id as the responsible step and record that the delivery step asserted the flagged claim even though the tool observations contradict it or provide no support for it.",
              "not_when": "Do not reattribute when the judge found no hallucination in the delivered result; do not reattribute when the delivered claim is fully supported by the tool observations; and do not move attribution to the delivery step when the flagged claim appears first, verbatim, inside an intermediate tool observation that the delivery step only reproduced unchanged, in which case the step whose observation introduced the claim remains responsible."
            },
            "claim": {
              "expected_behavior": "On judge-flagged cases in this family, the step tracer names the assistant delivery step (final answer tool call or last prose event asserting the flagged claim) with its event id as the responsible step, instead of naming search, retrieval, or code-execution steps that gathered data but did not author the flagged claim.",
              "target_polarity": "boundary",
              "target_kind": "localization"
            },
